Warp's Apache Cassandra frontend (Warp/src/main/java/com/sayonora/wire/cqlwire/) implements the CQL native protocol (versions 3 and 4) and the CQL language
subset described in docs/WARP_GUIDE.md; no Apache Cassandra source code is included. Its behaviour (result and error semantics, the Murmur3 partitioner token,
clustering order, system_schema layout) follows Apache Cassandra 5.0, and is verified by replaying, against Warp, answers recorded from a real
Apache Cassandra 5.0 container (Apache License, Version 2.0, Copyright The Apache Software Foundation, https://cassandra.apache.org): the recorded answers are
Warp/tests/python/cql_conformance/golden.json.gz and were produced with the DataStax python-driver (Apache License 2.0), which is a test-time dependency and is
not redistributed. The Apache License 2.0 text is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 .


Warp's Apache Kafka frontend (Warp/src/main/java/com/sayonora/wire/kafkawire/) implements the Kafka wire protocol (request versions listed by its ApiVersions
answer) and the broker-side behaviour described in docs/WARP_GUIDE.md; no Apache Kafka source code is included. Its message layouts follow the Kafka protocol
message definitions and its behaviour (error codes, offsets and watermarks, consumer group state machine, defaults of the topic configurations) follows Apache
Kafka 4.3, and is verified by replaying, against Warp, answers recorded from a real Apache Kafka container (Apache License, Version 2.0, Copyright The Apache
Software Foundation, https://kafka.apache.org): the recorded answers are Warp/tests/python/kafka_conformance/golden.json.gz and were produced with kafka-python
(Apache License 2.0), whose bundled copy of the Kafka protocol message definitions is also used by the test-time raw client (Warp/tests/python/kafka_conformance/kafka_raw_client.py).
Neither is redistributed. The Apache License 2.0 text is at https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0 .
